  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Oh Hell. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Oh Hell (also known as Oh Hell!) is a classic trick-taking card game that emphasizes precision bidding over raw power. Unlike most trick-takers where you try to win as many tricks as possible, the goal is to win exactly the number of tricks you bid. It is famous for its 'River' structure, where hand sizes increase and decrease throughout the game, and its 'Hook' rule that prevents every player from being successful simultaneously.",
    objective: 'Score the most points by winning EXACTLY the number of tricks you bid.',
    gameplay: "Play starts with the player to the dealer's left leading any card. Players must follow suit if able; otherwise they may play any card including trump. Highest trump wins the trick, or if no trump was played, highest card of the led suit wins. The trick winner leads to the next trick; play continues until all tricks are complete.",
    keyRules: [
      'Bid the exact number of tricks you will take; scoring only for making the bid exactly.',
      'Follow suit if able; if void, may play any card including trump.',
      'Trump is determined by the card turned after the deal; highest trump or highest of led suit wins the trick.',
      'The Hook: dealer may not bid so that total bids equal the number of tricks in the hand.',
      'Hand sizes follow the River: start at 10 (or 8/7 by player count), decrease to 1, then increase back.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'From 3 to 7 people can play. The game is best when played with 4 to 6.',
      deck: '52 cards. Rank: A > K > Q > J > 10... > 2.',
      equipment: '52 cards. Rank: A > K > Q > J > 10... > 2.',
      dealing: 'Varies by round. Round 1: 1 card each. Round 2: 2 cards each. (Ascending up to 10 or 12, then descending back to 1).',
    },
    turnFlow: "Play starts with the player to the dealer's left leading any card. Players must follow suit if able; otherwise they may play any card including trump. Highest trump wins the trick, or if no trump was played, highest card of the led suit wins. The trick winner leads to the next trick; play continues until all tricks are complete.",
